    description: "Found by the 2026-11-24 docstring staleness audit (dev 7e204b35b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11242026/review and verify). Corpus impact not measured. _extract_field_types_cpp stores a smart-pointer field's unwrapped pointee (cpp.py:600-614) and _cpp_receiver_class returns it whatever the operator (cpp.py:2046-2047). Field std::unique_ptr<Impl> impl_: impl_.get() binds Impl::get (receiver=declared_type). The same call on a parameter does not; the module docstring says a smart pointer's own . member is not the pointee's. r20, v04."  # c678
